  "body": "## Why\n\n`nix-bundle-dir` main changes what lands inside the AppDir: psABI interpreter at build time, `DT_RPATH` instead of `DT_RUNPATH`, no more `ld.so` trampoline / `libprocself_fix.so`, and a `bin/<name>` launcher only for GUI bundles that need `XKB_CONFIG_ROOT` or `QT_QPA_PLATFORMTHEME`. It also adds `qtCliApp`, which this flake mirrors automatically via `mapAttrs`.\n\nThis repo had **no CI**. The failure modes (a payload that cannot exec on another distro, a launcher whose companion ELF was not copied, a missing lib dir) all still build and still extract.\n\n## What\n\n- Bump `nix-bundle-dir` lock to `cb9afc8` (main).\n- Add `tests/smoke.sh`: two tiny AppImages \u2014 `hello` via `qtCliApp` (plain binaries) and `xkbcli` via `qtApp` (launcher + companion) \u2014 assert the payload contract inside the extracted AppDir, then run each in ubuntu and fedora containers with `APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1`.\n- Add `.github/workflows/ci.yml` on `ubuntu-latest` + `ubuntu-24.04-arm`.\n\nVerified against the pre-bump pin: 8 of these assertions fail there (9 on x86_64). The `cp -a ${bundle}/bin/.` vs `bin/*` question was settled by experiment \u2014 mutating it to `bin/*` produces an AppImage that builds, extracts, and then fails to run, which the new test catches.\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
