  "body": "AppImages FUSE-mount the embedded squashfs and read blocks on every page fault during app startup. For large Qt apps like Logos Basecamp, dlopen'ing Qt libraries, QML plugins, and module .so files reads many distinct blocks cold, and any compressor (gzip, zstd, etc.) makes each read pay CPU decompression cost \u2014 stretching cold startup into the minutes.\r\n\r\nDisable all four squashfs compression layers (-noI -noD -noF -noX) so reads through squashfuse are effectively pass-through. The resulting AppImage is larger on disk, but launch time is near-native: the common case (launching the app) should not pay a cost users notice, even if distribution size goes up.",
